**Policy Document: Creative Media Buying, Targeting, and Measurement**

**Effective Date:** January 1, 2024  
**Policy Number:** MKT-2024-CMBT-001  
**Reviewed by:** Sarah Thompson, Chief Marketing Officer  
**Approval Date:** December 15, 2023  

**1. Purpose**  
This policy outlines the procedures and guidelines for the creative media buying, targeting, and measurement processes at Powell Media Group (PMG) to ensure alignment with our strategic marketing goals.

**2. Definitions**  
- **Creative Media:** Includes all visual, audio, and digital content created for advertising purposes.
- **Media Buying:** The process of purchasing advertising space across various channels such as television, radio, digital platforms, and print.
- **Targeting:** The identification and segmentation of specific audiences to optimize advertising effectiveness.
- **Measurement:** The evaluation of campaign performance through analytics and key performance indicators (KPIs).

**3. Procedures**  

**3.1 Creative Development**  
The Creative Team, led by Emily Chen, will develop all advertising content. Projects must be submitted through the Creative Workflow System (CWS) at least 6 weeks prior to launch dates. All creatives must adhere to brand guidelines set forth by the Brand Management Team.

**3.2 Media Buying Process**  
Media buying will be conducted by the Media Buying Department, under the supervision of Mark Lopez. PMG will collaborate with external partners such as AdMetrics International for programmatic buying and Nielsen for audience measurement. All media buys must be approved by the Finance Department, led by John Carter, ensuring adherence to budgetary constraints.

**3.3 Targeting Strategy**  
Targeting efforts will be managed by the Data Analytics Team, with oversight from Laura Kim. Audience segments must be defined using the Audience Insight Tool (AIT), which integrates data from sources such as Facebook Ads Manager and Google Analytics. Segmentation must be reviewed quarterly to ensure relevance.

**3.4 Measurement and Reporting**  
Campaign performance will be assessed using the PMG Performance Dashboard, which consolidates data from various platforms including Adobe Analytics and HubSpot. Monthly reports will be generated by the Analytics Team, with insights presented to the Executive Board during the quarterly review meetings.

**4. Compliance**  
